<!--
  DJI 9450, 24 x 12.7 cm (9.4 x 5.0 in), the propeller of the DJI E305 system (E305 User Manual v1.0, Specifications).
  Static level: UIUC's static test of the DJI Phantom 3 9450 plastic propeller, C_T 0.1033 and C_P 0.0394, the means of
  its 5000-8000 rpm points, read from the vector data of Fig. 31 of Deters, Kleinke and Selig, "Static Testing of
  Propulsion Elements for Small Multirotor Unmanned Aerial Vehicles", AIAA 2017-3743
  (https://m-selig.ae.illinois.edu/pubs/DetersKleinkeSelig-2017-AIAA-Paper-2017-3743.pdf). Its coefficients are on the
  9.45 in (24.0 cm) diameter UIUC measured, DJI's 24 cm, used below. That this Phantom 3 blade is the E305's Z-Blade 9450 moulding is not confirmed.
  No advance-ratio sweep of the 9450 was found, so the fall-off with J is that of the APC 9x4.5E measured in UIUC's
  propeller database volume 1 (static run rd0995, dynamic run jb0998 at 6018 rpm, a straight line past its last point to
  zero thrust), scaled to the static level above and stretched in J by the pitch-to-diameter ratio (5.0/9.4)/(4.5/9).
-->
